UISelectable:bCanNavigateHere {
    at    Source/DreamGUIInput/Public/Interaction/UISelectable.h#UISelectable:bCanNavigateHere
    src   "Can we navigate from other selectable object to this one?\nIf other selectable use EUISelectableNavigationMode.Explicit and use this selectable as specific one, then this selectable can still be navigate to."
    text  "能否从其他可选中对象导航到此对象？\n如果其他可选中对象使用 EUISelectableNavigationMode.Explicit 并将此可选中对象指定为具体目标，则仍然可以导航到此可选中对象。"
    state machine
}

UISelectable:bInteractable {
    at    Source/DreamGUIInput/Public/Interaction/UISelectable.h#UISelectable:bInteractable
    src   "This control's own enabled flag. False draws it Disabled and refuses press, select, click and\nclick feedback; hover enter/exit still arrive, so a tooltip can say why it is off.\n\nDistinct from UDreamWidget::SetInteractable, which turns the RAYCAST off for a whole subtree.\nThis one leaves the widget hit-testable -- a disabled button still stops a click reaching the\npanel behind it, which is what a disabled button is for."
    text  "此控件自身的启用标志。为 false 时将其绘制为禁用状态，并拒绝按下、选中、点击和\n点击反馈；悬停进入/离开仍会触发，因此工具提示可以说明它为何处于关闭状态。\n\n与 UDreamWidget::SetInteractable 不同，后者会关闭整个子树的 RAYCAST。\n此标志仍让控件可被命中测试——禁用的按钮仍会阻止点击到达\n其后的面板，这正是禁用按钮的用途。"
    state machine
}

UISelectable:bUseFocusedVisuals {
    at    Source/DreamGUIInput/Public/Interaction/UISelectable.h#UISelectable:bUseFocusedVisuals
    src   "Give keyboard and gamepad focus a look of its own. Off, a focused control wears the Hovered\nvisuals -- what every control authored before focus was a separate state already expects."
    text  "让键盘和手柄焦点拥有独立的外观。关闭时，获得焦点的控件沿用悬停\n视觉效果——这也是在焦点成为独立状态之前创建的所有控件所期望的。"
    state machine
}

UISelectable:bUseFocusRing {
    at    Source/DreamGUIInput/Public/Interaction/UISelectable.h#UISelectable:bUseFocusRing
    src   "Mark this control's focus with the screen's focus ring (the project's NavigationSelectionClass) while that focus is\ndrawn. Off for a control whose own look marks its focus -- a row that turns dark, a tab that rises -- so no ring\ndraws a second mark over it; the focus moving onto such a control takes the ring away with it rather than leaving\nit on the control the focus came from."
    text  "在绘制焦点时，用屏幕的焦点环（项目的 NavigationSelectionClass）标记此控件的焦点。\n对于自身外观已标记焦点的控件——例如变暗的行、抬起的选项卡——请关闭此项，\n以免焦点环在其上再画一重标记；焦点移到这类控件上时，焦点环会随之移走，\n而不会留在焦点来源的控件上。"
    state machine
}

UISelectable:ClickMethod {
    at    Source/DreamGUIInput/Public/Interaction/UISelectable.h#UISelectable:ClickMethod
    src   "WHEN this control's click fires, per input kind -- UMG's three, and resolved the way UMG's\nSButton resolves them: the active input device picks which of the three is asked.\n\nHeld here rather than on UUIButton because a check box, a tab and a list row all want the same\nanswer and none of them is a UUIButton; the CLICKERS (UUIButton, UUIToggle) are what consult\nthem, through ShouldClickOn* below. A selectable that does not click (a slider, a scroll bar)\nsimply never asks."
    text  "此控件的点击在何时触发，按输入类型区分——即 UMG 的三种类型，解析方式与 UMG 的\nSButton 相同：由当前活动的输入设备决定询问哪一种。\n\n这些设置放在此处而非 UUIButton 上，是因为复选框、选项卡和列表行都需要相同的\n答案，而它们都不是 UUIButton；真正查询它们的是点击者（UUIButton、UUIToggle），\n通过下方的 ShouldClickOn* 进行。不处理点击的可选中控件（滑块、滚动条）\n则根本不会询问。"
    state machine
}

UISelectable:GetCurrentSelectionState {
    at    Source/DreamGUIInput/Public/Interaction/UISelectable.h#UISelectable:GetCurrentSelectionState
    src   "The state IN EFFECT -- the one the transition was last run for and the one on screen.\n\nGetSelectionState above DERIVES a state from the pointer flags; this is the one that was applied.\nEvery pointer event assigns the first to the second, so under real input they agree. They part\nwhen something drives SetSelectionState directly, and then this is the honest answer to \"does it\nlook pressed\": it is what a control asked whether it IS pressed should read."
    text  "生效中的状态——即最后一次运行过渡所依据的状态，也是屏幕上呈现的状态。\n\n上方的 GetSelectionState 根据指针标志推导出一个状态；这里返回的是实际应用的那个状态。\n每次指针事件都会把前者赋给后者，因此在真实输入下二者一致。当有代码直接驱动\nSetSelectionState 时二者便会分开，此时它才是“看起来是否被按下”的可靠答案：\n控件在被询问是否确实处于按下状态时应当读取它。"
    state machine
}

